Morning all,

As agreed on Friday, please leave the HOLD tag attached to any first-off box =
still on the hold rack when the shift changes, starting today on Trafford T2 =
and Warrington W1. At handover, please tell the incoming lead in person which=
 boxes are still open. Show them the tag and say which check is outstanding.

The receiving lead should match the tag and all three sheets to the job instr=
uction and record the approval time when the check passes. Keep the box on th=
e rack until it can actually go back to good stock. At that move, the receivi=
ng lead should be there to sign the tag and enter the actual return date and =
time. Please update the same register row against the original run and event.=
 If the tag is missing, the specification differs or approval is still outsta=
nding, keep the box on hold and tell Gareth on T2 or Martin on W1.

I've attached the briefing PDF for both shifts and the hold tag register as a=
 separate workbook. The PDF shows the route back to the rack if a check fails=
. The workbook has an Example tab showing why the approval and return times h=
ave separate fields. Gareth and Martin, please use the Register tab for the l=
ive boxes from today.

Thanks,
Siobhan

